      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled dose. The usual maximums are 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A single 1,700 mg dose is also above the usual maximum per dose of about 1,000 mg. At this level the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up significantly.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg PO once daily.** This is 1,700 mg/day, though a single dose that size isn't standard either. It would more often be split, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **Another dose.** Tell me the dose and frequency you want.\n\nIf you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that it's intentional. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it."
